# Oxidoc Skills for AI Agents

AI coding agents like Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor have no built-in knowledge of Oxidoc. These ready-made skill prompts give them everything they need — paste one into your agent's context and it can create, edit, and build Oxidoc sites.

## How to Use

1. Copy the skill prompt you need
2. Paste it into your AI agent's instructions:
   - **Claude Code** — add to `CLAUDE.md` in your project root
   - **Cursor** — add to `.cursorrules`
   - **Codex** — add to `AGENTS.md`
   - **Windsurf** — add to `.windsurfrules`
   - **Other** — paste into the system prompt or project instructions

## Full Oxidoc Skill

This single prompt covers the CLI, RDX syntax, configuration, and components. Copy the entire block.

<Accordion title="Full Oxidoc Skill — click to expand">

<CodeBlock language="markdown" filename="CLAUDE.md">
# Oxidoc Documentation Engine

## What is Oxidoc
Oxidoc is a documentation engine written in Rust. It generates static documentation sites from `.rdx` files (Markdown with embedded components). Zero Node.js dependency — single binary.

## CLI Commands

```bash
# Initialize a new project
oxidoc init my-docs

# Start dev server with hot reload (default port 3000)
oxidoc dev
oxidoc dev -p 8080

# Build for production (output to dist/)
oxidoc build
oxidoc build -o public

# Remove build artifacts
oxidoc clean

# Version management
oxidoc archive create v1.0    # Snapshot current docs
oxidoc archive list            # List archived versions
oxidoc archive delete v1.0    # Delete an archive
oxidoc update                  # Update to latest stable
oxidoc update --pre            # Update to latest prerelease
oxidoc set-version v0.1.0     # Pin specific version

# Global flags
# -C <path>   Project directory
# -v          Verbose output
# -q          Quiet (errors only)
```

## RDX File Format

RDX files are Markdown with YAML frontmatter and embedded components:

```rdx
---
title: Page Title
description: Meta description for SEO (150-160 chars)
layout: landing  # Optional: removes sidebar for landing pages
---

# Heading

Standard **Markdown** with [links](url), `code`, lists, tables, etc.

<Callout kind="info" title="Note">
Callout content. Kinds: info, warning, error/danger, tip/success.
</Callout>

<Tabs>
<Tab title="Tab 1">Content one</Tab>
<Tab title="Tab 2">Content two</Tab>
</Tabs>

<CodeBlock language="rust" filename="main.rs" highlight="2">
fn main() {
    println!("Hello!");
}
</CodeBlock>

<Accordion title="Click to expand">
Hidden content.
</Accordion>

<CardGrid>
<Card title="Card" icon="🚀" href="/link">Description.</Card>
</CardGrid>

<Steps>
<Step title="First">Do this.</Step>
<Step title="Second">Then this.</Step>
</Steps>

<Badge variant="new">New</Badge>
<Badge variant="deprecated">Deprecated</Badge>
<Tag variant="experimental">experimental</Tag>
<Tooltip text="Explanation here">hover text</Tooltip>

<Banner id="unique-id" persist="session">
Announcement text.
</Banner>

<ThemedImage light="/light.png" dark="/dark.png" alt="Logo" />

<Head>
<meta property="og:image" content="/social-card.png">
</Head>
```

Mermaid diagrams use fenced code blocks with `mermaid` language.

## Landing Page Components

Set `layout: landing` in frontmatter, then use:

```rdx
<Hero title="Project Name">
<HeroAction label="Get Started" href="/docs/quickstart" variant="primary" />
<HeroAction label="GitHub" href="https://github.com/..." variant="secondary" />
Tagline text here.
</Hero>

<Section bg="muted">
<FeatureGrid>
<Feature icon="⚡" title="Fast">Description.</Feature>
</FeatureGrid>
</Section>

<CTA title="Ready?" description="Get started now.">
<HeroAction label="Install" href="/docs/install" variant="primary" />
</CTA>

<TestimonialGrid>
<Testimonial name="Jane" role="Dev">Great tool.</Testimonial>
</TestimonialGrid>
```

## Configuration (oxidoc.toml)

```toml
[project]
name = "Project Name"
description = "Site description for SEO"
logo = "/assets/logo.svg"
favicon = "/assets/favicon.svg"
base_url = "https://example.com"
edit_url = "https://github.com/org/repo/blob/main"
edit_label = "Edit this page"

[theme]
primary = "#3b82f6"
accent = "#f59e0b"
font = "Inter, sans-serif"
code_font = "JetBrains Mono, monospace"
dark_mode = "system"  # "system", "light", or "dark"
custom_css = ["assets/custom.css"]

[routing.root]
homepage = "home.rdx"
# pages = ["about.rdx"]

[routing]
header_links = [
  { label = "Docs", href = "/docs" },
  { label = "API", href = "/api" },
]
navigation = [
  { path = "/docs", dir = "docs", groups = [
    { group = "Getting Started", pages = ["quickstart", "guide"] },
    { group = "Advanced", pages = ["config", "plugins"] },
  ] },
  { path = "/api", openapi = "./openapi.yaml" },
]

[search]
# provider = "oxidoc"  # Default, zero-config BM25 search
# semantic = true       # Enable semantic search
# For Algolia: provider = "algolia", app_id, api_key, index_name
# For Typesense: provider = "typesense", host, port, protocol, api_key, collection_name
# For Meilisearch: provider = "meilisearch", host, api_key, index_name

[versioning]
# default = "v2.0"
# versions = ["v1.0", "v2.0"]

[i18n]
# default_locale = "en"
# locales = ["en", "ja", "es"]
# translation_dir = "i18n"

[footer]
copyright_owner = "Your Name"
# links = [{ label = "Privacy", href = "/privacy" }]

[social]
github = "https://github.com/org/repo"
# discord = "https://discord.gg/invite"

[analytics]
# google_analytics = "G-XXXXXXXXXX"
# script = '<script defer src="https://plausible.io/js/script.js"></script>'

[redirects]
# redirects = [{ from = "/old", to = "/new" }]

[components.custom]
# MyWidget = "assets/js/my-widget.js"

[attribution]
oxidoc = true  # "Built with Oxidoc" in footer
```

## File Structure

```
project/
├── oxidoc.toml        # Configuration
├── home.rdx           # Landing page (layout: landing)
├── assets/            # Static assets (copied to dist/)
├── docs/              # Content directory
│   ├── intro.rdx
│   ├── guide.rdx
│   └── advanced/
│       └── plugins.rdx
└── i18n/              # Translation files (if i18n enabled)
    ├── en.ftl
    └── ja.ftl
```

## Auto-Generated Output

`oxidoc build` produces in `dist/`:
- Static HTML for every page
- Wasm islands for interactive components
- Search index (chunked for lazy loading)
- sitemap.xml, robots.txt, feed.xml
- llms.txt, llms-full.txt (for AI/RAG)
- Redirect HTML files (if configured)

## Key Rules
- Content files use `.rdx` extension (NOT `.md` or `.mdx`)
- Components use PascalCase: `<Callout>`, `<CodeBlock>`, `<CardGrid>`
- Pages appear in sidebar only if listed in navigation groups
- CSS overrides use `--oxidoc-*` variables (e.g., `--oxidoc-primary`)
- Custom CSS always wins over built-in styles (no !important needed)
- The `<Head>` component injects custom HTML into `<head>`
- **Code blocks:** Use standard fenced code blocks (```lang) for plain code. Only use `<CodeBlock>` when you need `filename`, `highlight`, or `line_numbers` props. Example:
  - Plain code → ```bash\noxidoc build\n```
  - With filename → `<CodeBlock language="toml" filename="oxidoc.toml">...</CodeBlock>`
  - With highlighting → `<CodeBlock language="rust" highlight="2">...</CodeBlock>`
</CodeBlock>

</Accordion>

## Skill: RDX Content Writer

Focused on writing `.rdx` content pages. Use this when you only need the agent to create or edit documentation content, not configure the site.

<Accordion title="RDX Content Writer Skill — click to expand">

<CodeBlock language="markdown" filename="CLAUDE.md">
# RDX Content Writing

## Format
RDX files are Markdown with YAML frontmatter and embedded components. Extension: `.rdx`

## Frontmatter (required)
```yaml
---
title: Page Title — Descriptive Hook | Brand
description: 150-160 char meta description with action verb and CTA.
---
```

## Code Blocks
Use standard fenced code blocks (```lang) for plain code snippets.
Only use `<CodeBlock>` component when you need `filename`, `highlight`, or `line_numbers` props:
- Plain: ```bash\noxidoc build\n```
- With filename: `<CodeBlock language="toml" filename="oxidoc.toml">content</CodeBlock>`
- With highlight: `<CodeBlock language="rust" highlight="2">content</CodeBlock>`

## Available Components

Callout: `<Callout kind="info|warning|error|tip" title="Title">Content</Callout>`
Tabs: `<Tabs><Tab title="Label">Content</Tab></Tabs>`
CodeBlock: `<CodeBlock language="rust" filename="file.rs" highlight="2">code</CodeBlock>` (only with filename/highlight/line_numbers)
Accordion: `<Accordion title="Label">Content</Accordion>`
CardGrid: `<CardGrid><Card title="T" icon="🚀" href="/link">Desc</Card></CardGrid>`
Steps: `<Steps><Step title="First">Content</Step></Steps>`
Badge: `<Badge variant="new|deprecated|tip|warning|danger">Label</Badge>`
Tag: `<Tag variant="new|experimental|deprecated">label</Tag>`
Tooltip: `<Tooltip text="Explanation">hover text</Tooltip>`
Banner: `<Banner id="unique" persist="none|session|forever">Text</Banner>`
ThemedImage: `<ThemedImage light="/l.png" dark="/d.png" alt="Alt" />`
Head: `<Head><meta property="og:image" content="/img.png"></Head>`

Mermaid: use fenced code block with `mermaid` language.

## SEO Rules
- Title: under 60 chars, front-load keyword, format "Primary — Hook | Brand"
- Description: 150-160 chars, action verb, unique per page
- First paragraph = meta description (auto-extracted, max 160 chars)
- Every page must have unique title and description

## Markdown
Standard Markdown: headings (#-######), bold, italic, links, images, lists, tables, code blocks, blockquotes, horizontal rules. Headings auto-generate anchor links.
</CodeBlock>

</Accordion>

## Skill: Oxidoc CLI Operator

For CI/CD automation or when the agent needs to run Oxidoc commands.

<Accordion title="CLI Operator Skill — click to expand">

<CodeBlock language="markdown" filename="CLAUDE.md">
# Oxidoc CLI

Binary: `oxidoc` (single binary, no runtime deps)

## Install
```bash
curl -fsSL https://oxidoc.dev/install.sh | sh
```

## Commands
```
oxidoc init [name]              Create new project (-f force, -y skip prompts)
oxidoc dev [-p port]            Dev server with hot reload (default: 3000)
oxidoc build [-o dir]           Production build (default output: dist/)
oxidoc clean                    Remove .oxidoc-dev/ and dist/
oxidoc archive create <ver>     Snapshot docs as version archive
oxidoc archive list             List archives
oxidoc archive delete <ver>     Delete archive
oxidoc update [--pre]           Update binary (--pre for prerelease)
oxidoc set-version <ver>        Pin specific version
```

## Global Flags
```
-C, --project <path>    Project root directory
-v, --verbose           Detailed output
-q, --quiet             Errors only (CI mode)
```

## CI Example (GitHub Actions)
```yaml
- run: curl -fsSL https://oxidoc.dev/install.sh | sh
- run: oxidoc build
```

## Output
`oxidoc build` generates a fully static site in dist/ — HTML, CSS, JS, Wasm, search index, sitemap, llms.txt. Serve with any static host.
</CodeBlock>

</Accordion>

## Skill: Oxidoc Site Configurator

For when the agent needs to set up or modify `oxidoc.toml`.

<Accordion title="Site Configurator Skill — click to expand">

<CodeBlock language="markdown" filename="CLAUDE.md">
# Oxidoc Configuration (oxidoc.toml)

## Minimal Config
```toml
[project]
name = "My Docs"

[routing.root]
homepage = "home.rdx"

[routing]
navigation = [
  { path = "/docs", dir = "docs", groups = [
    { group = "Guide", pages = ["intro", "quickstart"] },
  ] },
]
```

## All Sections

[project] — name (required), description, logo, base_url, edit_url, edit_label, debug_islands
[theme] — primary, accent, font, code_font, dark_mode ("system"|"light"|"dark"), custom_css
[routing.root] — homepage (rdx file), pages (additional root pages)
[routing] — header_links [{label, href}], navigation [{path, dir, groups [{group, pages}], openapi}]
[search] — provider ("oxidoc"|"algolia"|"typesense"|"meilisearch"|"custom"), semantic (bool), model_path
  Algolia: app_id, api_key, index_name
  Typesense: host, port, protocol, api_key, collection_name
  Meilisearch: host, api_key, index_name
  Custom: stylesheet, script, init_script
[versioning] — default, versions
[i18n] — default_locale, locales, translation_dir
[footer] — copyright_owner, copyright_owner_url, links [{label, href}]
[social] — github, discord, twitter, mastodon
[analytics] — google_analytics, script
[redirects] — redirects [{from, to}]
[components.custom] — TagName = "path/to/file.js"
[attribution] — oxidoc (bool, default true)

## Navigation Rules
- `path` = URL prefix ("/docs", "/api")
- `dir` = content directory for .rdx files
- `groups` = sidebar sections, each with `group` (title) and `pages` (slug list)
- `openapi` = path to OpenAPI spec (auto-generates API pages)
- Pages must be listed in groups to appear in sidebar
- Nested pages: "guides/styling" maps to docs/guides/styling.rdx
</CodeBlock>

</Accordion>

## Skill: Oxidoc Theme Customizer

For when the agent needs to customize the visual design.

<Accordion title="Theme Customizer Skill — click to expand">

<CodeBlock language="markdown" filename="CLAUDE.md">
# Oxidoc Theming

## Quick (oxidoc.toml)
```toml
[theme]
primary = "#3b82f6"
accent = "#f59e0b"
dark_mode = "system"
custom_css = ["assets/custom.css"]
```

## CSS Variables (override in custom CSS)
All styles use `@layer oxidoc` — your CSS always wins, no !important needed.

Core: --oxidoc-primary, --oxidoc-accent, --oxidoc-bg, --oxidoc-bg-secondary, --oxidoc-text, --oxidoc-text-secondary, --oxidoc-border, --oxidoc-code-bg
Semantic: --oxidoc-success, --oxidoc-warning, --oxidoc-error, --oxidoc-info, --oxidoc-new, --oxidoc-deprecated (each has -text variant)
Utility: --oxidoc-text-muted, --oxidoc-bg-subtle, --oxidoc-on-primary, --oxidoc-shadow, --oxidoc-overlay
Typography: --oxidoc-font-sans, --oxidoc-font-mono
Layout: --oxidoc-content-max (48rem), --oxidoc-sidebar-width (16rem), --oxidoc-toc-width (14rem), --oxidoc-header-height (3.5rem)
Radius: --oxidoc-radius-sm/md/lg
Shadows: --oxidoc-shadow-sm/md/lg
Z-index: --oxidoc-z-tooltip(10), z-back-to-top(50), z-sidebar(90), z-header(100), z-skip-nav(200), z-overlay(1000)
Transitions: --oxidoc-transition-fast/normal/slow/spring

## Dark mode
Override in `[data-theme="dark"]` selector. Primary shades auto-generate via color-mix().
```css
:root { --oxidoc-primary: #2563eb; }
[data-theme="dark"] { --oxidoc-primary: #3b82f6; }
```
</CodeBlock>

</Accordion>

## Combining Skills

You can combine multiple skill blocks in a single `CLAUDE.md` or `.cursorrules` file. For most projects, the **Full Oxidoc Skill** is all you need. Use the focused skills when you want to keep the agent's context lean.

<Callout kind="tip" title="Keep it updated">
When you upgrade Oxidoc, check this page for updated skill prompts. New components and config options get added to the skills as they ship.
</Callout>
